Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:53:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] A course has a syllabus, and a household reads only its
 own progress

syllabus_topics seeded from the portal's course_topics and edited by whoever
manages the course; a teacher's mark on a topic, written only by somebody
with a session for that child on that course this week; a report's topics;
child_progress, which gathers the signals (lessons, practice, tests, marks,
weekly volume, accuracy, attendance, reports) the room turns into statuses
with its own rule; lesson_brief_facts, the pre-lesson brief's reads,
including the last three published reports by any teacher (a widening for
the owner to approve); the no-join sweep that files one task per lesson;
and recording retention (recording_months, default 3).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
